\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs21 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs21\insrsid10694274 \hich\af2\dbch\af0\loch\f2 o\tab}After experimenting with a parameter, you can }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid10694274\charrsid10694274 
keep the parameter value giving the best results}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10694274  and go ahead with experimenting with the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid10694274\charrsid10694274 next parameter}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid10694274 
. You can include the results obtained with the best value in the previous parameter as the results with the default value in the current parameter you are experimenting with. For example, after experimenting with the activation of the hidden layers, if y
ou find that ReLU performed best, you can keep this value for the activation function of the hidden layers 
and include its corresponding results in the default value for the following experiments regarding the activation function of the output layer when you start experimenting with it.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs21 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs21\insrsid10694274 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar
\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa160\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls4\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid10694274 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10694274 
Each parameter has a number of required experiments indicated by the index after the \'93-\'93 in the parameter name. Each experiment corresponds to trying out a different parameter value than those in the experiments before; with experiment \'93-1\'94
 corresponding to the default parameter value.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs21 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs21\insrsid10694274 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
For each optimizer, you need to experiment with different hyperparameters (at least two different experiments), so you will find for each optimizer experiment index, two sub-indices. For example, experiment 1.1 in optimizers is SGD with learning rate = 0.
1, experiment 1.2 should be SGD with other learning rate and hyperparameter values and so on.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs21 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs21\insrsid10694274 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Similar to the previous point, for each filter size, you need to experiment with different stride lengths}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 
